WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.220
You know the gist: 13 years in the&nbsp;
making, new technology, underwater,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:09.960
yada yada yada — but what do the fans have&nbsp;
to say about Avatar: The Way of Water?

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:15.840
The second installment in the Avatar franchise&nbsp;
was released internationally on December 15th,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:19.860
and those who rushed out to see the sequel&nbsp;
are now giving their reviews on Twitter.

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:24.720
James Cameron had a lot on his plate with&nbsp;
the movie, but the director certainly isn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.460
afraid of a challenge. There is at least&nbsp;
one more sequel on the way after The Way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:34.140
of Water and possibly additional Avatar flicks&nbsp;
coming if everyone is happy with number two.

00:00:34.529 --> 00:00:39.300
"The day we deliver Avatar 2, we'll just&nbsp;
start working on finishing Avatar 3."

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:45.420
So, are they happy? Well, those lucky enough to&nbsp;
have seen the film already certainly are, so there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:50.280
is a lot to look forward to from Cameron in the&nbsp;
decade ahead. Let's get straight to it — finding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.280 --> 00:00:56.340
a negative reaction to Avatar: The Way of Water&nbsp;
is no easy feat. As one Twitter user posted:

00:01:07.363 --> 00:01:08.820
Meanwhile, another said:

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:20.400
Some were going as far as to name Avatar:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:24.360
The Way of Water the best movie&nbsp;
they'd ever seen. One tweet read:

00:01:34.867 --> 00:01:38.280
Another moviegoer compared&nbsp;
the Avatar sequel to other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:42.780
recent underwater flicks… and it's&nbsp;
clear one reigns supreme. They said:

00:01:55.680 --> 00:02:01.260
It's hard to find someone who straight-up hated&nbsp;
Avatar: The Way of Water, but some people do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:07.320
seem to take exception to the movie's lengthy&nbsp;
192-minute runtime. As one Twitter user posted:

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:20.820
Many Twitter users mentioned that the&nbsp;
film was a little too long in their posts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:24.060
but they often followed up with&nbsp;
a compliment. One user said:

00:02:29.463 --> 00:02:30.423
Another wrote:

00:02:36.360 --> 00:02:40.080
If three-hour films aren't a&nbsp;
problem for you, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:43.140
it seems like you won't have any&nbsp;
complaints about The Way of Water.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:48.120
One person even claimed you won't notice&nbsp;
the three-hour-plus runtime, writing:

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:01.380
So, if you loved the first Avatar, you&nbsp;
should be thrilled with The Way of Water.

00:03:01.696 --> 00:03:03.436
"I see you."

00:03:03.595 --> 00:03:05.095
"I see you."

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:10.080
Twitter users have praised everything from&nbsp;
the movie's visuals to its 3D technology,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:14.940
while pointing out that the story is more&nbsp;
complex than the first movie. Many pointed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:19.740
out that the movie's themes and characters were&nbsp;
particularly compelling. As one Twitter user said:

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:32.640
There were plenty of tweets praising Zoe&nbsp;
Saldana's Neytiri in particular, which is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:38.460
no surprise given she's a standout in the original&nbsp;
film. Jake and Neytiri's children also seem to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:43.320
a highlight — and, naturally, you should also&nbsp;
be ready to shed some tears. One poster said:

00:03:54.342 --> 00:03:57.780
All in all, The Way of Water&nbsp;
appears to be worth the wait,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.780 --> 00:04:02.160
and moviegoers are likely to have one of&nbsp;
their best theater experiences of the year.

